<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrius the Fair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 250 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrius the Fair was a Macedonian prince, son of Demetrius I Poliorcetes and half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-ii-gonatas">Antigonus II Gonatas</a>. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas of Cyrene</a> around 250 BCE, the widowed queen Apama invited him to marry her daughter Berenice and rule Cyrene, undoing Magas's plan to reunite it with Ptolemaic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. He became Apama's lover, and Berenice had him killed.</p></div>
